CONVERSATION:
so this swapCache is causing all sorts of weird issues for me
iis it possible to clear out whatevers in cache manifest?
chrome://appcache-internals/ lets you delete caches
in chrome
no i mean programmatically
what are you using swapCache for? It's not something I'd imagine using often
okay
image an article website, with each article containing a &quot;save for offline&quot; button
server creates a CUSTOM browser unique Cache manifest for that particular users session
each user has a unqiue cache manifest depending on what articles he/she chose to cache
it works fine the first time
but the second time, it fails due to this appCache.swapCache();
if i remove it out it just tells me New cache available
I considered using custom manifests, but went with LocalStorage instead
I am using this to display the caching progress to the user http://www.bennadel.com/blog/2029-Using-HTML5-Offline-Application-Cache-Events-In-Javascript.htm
I do that too
I use local storage to store the article html
however there are many images, and that is what i use cache manifest for
Ohh, I see, the images
right
I'd be tempted to store those in LocalStorage too, as base64 :D
maybe too much data to put in localstorage though
right
I dont want to have to convert images and then decrypt them/....
and this cache manifest works great!   besides this exception
and if i remove it - my event for All files dfownloed never fires
so I was thinking - programmatically DELETE cache manifest and recache everything
So, send a request to the server in an iframe that says &quot;add these images to the cache&quot;, which returns an html page linking to the manifest
right thats what i do
the browser sees the updated manifest and caches the images
i dont use an iframe
I create the custom cvache manifest file then redirect to another page which references it and contains the evnt handlers
meh, you could do it with a full page refresh too
what do you need the event handlers for?
to display to the user that a cache i in progress
otherwise they will be tempted to navigate away from the caching page
fair enough
and the cache will not complete if they leave
and the caching fails?
I get some sort of  INVALID_STATE_ERR: DOM Exception 11
and i've been confused about it since days
trying to find compremises around it
does this error happen when you call swapCache?
yes
Ok‚Ä¶ why do you need to call swapCache?
I dont fully know :P
hah, don't call it then :D
however I believe its nessesary cause maybe the browser says &quot;hey some of this cache content is already cached, some im going to do something different&quot;
if I dont
some of the files dont get cached it seems
and maybe im wrong
nah, you only need swapCache() if you're going to stay on that page and make some additional requests
&quot;cached&quot;,       never fires
$( appCache ).bind( &quot;cached&quot;,        never fires UNLESS i do swapcache
so I cant successfully handle the event
What does Chrome's web inspector console tell you? It has some great debug info for appcache
the &quot;all files downloaded&quot; event
u mean the dev tools console output?
it just gives me that error
yep
Uncaught Error: INVALID_STATE_ERR: DOM Exception 11
‚Ä¶even if you don't call swapCache?
and points me to the line   $( appCache ).bind(    &quot;updateready&quot;,
if i dont call it I get no error
You don't get a &quot;Application Cache Checking event&quot; or anything?
yeah I do
I get UpdateReady event
Ok, what exactly does Chrome's web inspector console tell you?
okay so on the 1st article cache I get    no problems   &quot; Application Cache Cached event&quot;
the second time
I get &quot;Application Cache UpdateReady event
You don't see anything like &quot;Document was loaded from Application Cache with manifest...&quot;
or &quot;Application Cache Checking event&quot;
?
no
just anyway, thanks for listening
sometimes it helps just discribing the problem :P
Try testing in Chrome Canary, you might get better debugging info
sounds like you're missing some usual messages
also
something interesting
the first time i do it  first line says &quot; Creating Application Cache with manifest&quot;
second time it says &quot; Adding master entry to Application Cache with manifest&quot;
A master entry is something specifically listed in the cache
or maybe perhaps i can somehow modify the checking so it always downloads instead of looking for an update."")
